\toprule
Cohort & $n_\text{ref}$ & $n_\text{foc}$ & C\% & Null & Gen. \\
\midrule
Temporal (23v24) & 1080 & 807 & 31.3 & 12.4 & 18.9 \\
Ability quintile & 1044 & 1044 & 2.9 & 0.2 & 2.7 \\
Llama-2 vs. 3 & 161 & 308 & 61.3 & 38.2 & 23.1 \\
Random split & \multicolumn{2}{c}{(equal)} & 0.18 & -- & -- \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\paragraph{Architecture stratification.} METABENCH MMLU is 99.98\% decoder-only (5,226 of 5,227 models). Removing the single non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard = 1.0, C\% = 31.3\%). IRT fit diagnostics remain poor for both populations (RMSEA = 0.048--0.049, CFI = 0.71, TLI = 0.68), reflecting MMLU's 57-subject multidimensionality rather than architecture heterogeneity. Table~\ref{tab:irt_fit} reports these diagnostics.

