\subsection{Multi-Benchmark DIF Atlas} \label{sec:atlas}

We apply the same temporal DIF and permutation calibration pipeline to six benchmarks in METABENCH. Table~\ref{tab:atlas} reports raw C\%, permutation null, calibrated C\%, and random-split controls. Calibrated instability ranges from 7.3\% (HellaSwag) to 17.1\% (MMLU). All random controls are below 1\%, confirming that temporal structure produces genuine DIF beyond chance.

The cross-benchmark variation is 2.3$\times$ (7.3\% to 17.1\%). Item count correlates with raw C\% ($r = 0.72$), but permutation calibration partially accounts for this, as larger benchmarks also produce higher null rates. The rank order of benchmarks is preserved after calibration (Spearman $\rho = 0.886$ between raw and calibrated C\%).

